From 233adce9b327c013a8333f0cb9eb4230cfe78c10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Wuitz <dennish@wuitz.de>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:49:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libexpr: memoize rooted paths in the evaluation cache and
 batch validity checks

Once addTempRoot succeeded and the path was confirmed valid on the eval
store, the temporary root pins it for the lifetime of the store handle,
so re-rooting and re-validating it is a redundant round-trip. Track such
paths in EvalState::rootedValidPaths, root and check the remaining
context paths of a cached string with one addTempRoots and one
queryValidPaths instead of a pair of calls per path, and seed the memo
from derivationStrict where writeDerivation has just rooted and
registered the path.

On a daemon store this drops the dominant per-.drv AddTempRoot and
IsValidPath round-trip pairs during cached-string reads (~10x fewer hot
daemon ops on a cold flake walk that re-reads its own cache entries).
